# WP: "Seen by" under my latest message, in the real app against semaphore-fake-server (showcase).
# - A DM: Priya's client reads my message (the `read_receipt` control, which announces it to the
#   group as the backend's `markReadAndAnnounce` does) and the line names her, with no hover.
# - A newer message of mine moves the line: it never shows the older message's answer, and names
#   her again once she has read the new one.
# - A channel: the readers route answers when my message becomes the latest (channels send no
#   receipt events, so a channel's line is read once per message).

app 1280 800
click auth-connect
wait core label "Username" within 5
click auth-username
type "alexk"
click auth-password
type "hunter2"
click auth-login
wait core session signed-in
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
wait core connection connected
window activate

# 1. The DM with Priya: my message, then her read.
click rail-dm
wait core element dm-sidebar
click dm-row-$ID(dm-priya)
wait core dm $ID(dm-priya)
wait core element dm-header
type "seen check one"
press enter
wait core sent "seen check one"
wait core w9v seen none
server read_receipt "{\"dmGroupId\": \"$ID(dm-priya)\", \"userId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\"}"
wait core w9v seen "seen check one" "Seen by pri"
wait idle
shot 01-dm-seen

# 2. A newer message: the line leaves the old one and nothing is drawn until she reads this one.
# The fake server's clock only moves when told: a minute on, so her read is older than it.
server advance_clock "{\"ms\": 60000}"
type "seen check two"
press enter
wait core sent "seen check two"
wait core w9v seen none
expect core w9v seen none
server read_receipt "{\"dmGroupId\": \"$ID(dm-priya)\", \"userId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\"}"
wait core w9v seen "seen check two" "Seen by pri"
wait idle
shot 02-dm-moved

# 3. A channel: Priya's watermark is past what I send, so the readers route names her.
server read_receipt "{\"channelId\": \"$ID(cc-general)\", \"userId\": \"$ID(u-priya)\", \"at\": \"2030-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}"
navigate /community/$ID(c-couch)/channel/$ID(cc-general)
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
type "seen check channel"
press enter
wait core sent "seen check channel"
wait core w9v seen "seen check channel" "Seen by pri"
expect core requests ReadReceiptsController_getMessageReaders >= 1
wait idle
shot 03-channel-seen
